{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "workflow-title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Controlled scenario workflow\n## Proposed trusted runtime\nThe workbook calculates; the scenario tool operates only an analyst-approved contract and preserves the evidence.",
      "x": -275,
      "y": -400,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 1 · Known baseline\nSelect the intended workbook and saved baseline. The canonical workbook is not casually edited.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 2 · Verify identity and contract\nConfirm workbook identity, compatible version, expected sheets, mapped cells, and nearby structural fingerprints.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "isolate",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 3 · Isolate the run\nUse a controlled Excel session or working copy. Preserve the authoritative source workbook unchanged.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "snapshot",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 4 · Snapshot approved inputs\nRecord every current input value, calculation state, and required validation state before writing anything.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "write",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 5 · Write only to the allowlist\nValidate type, unit, range, and permitted values. Never select new inputs or alter formulas at runtime.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 1360,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "recalculate",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 6 · Let desktop Excel calculate\nUse the workbook's existing formulas and authoritative Excel runtime. AI is not the numerical engine.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 1700,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "capture",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 7 · Capture and validate\nCollect approved outputs, whole-workbook differences, calculation state, reconciliation cells, and validation results.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 2040,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "restore",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 8 · Restore or discard\nRestore every prior input and verify restoration, or discard the isolated copy. Fail closed if restoration cannot be proven.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 2380,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 9 · Save the scenario record\nStore the contract, baseline identity, inputs, outputs, differences, statuses, and run evidence separately from the workbook.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 2720,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "deliver",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 10 · Compare and communicate\nRerun or duplicate the scenario, compare it with baseline and other cases, and export a deliberate decision package.",
      "x": -250,
      "y": 3060,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "implemented-foundation",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Implemented today\nVersion 0.2.0 provides local save-by-save capture and workbook comparison. It does **not** execute or certify scenarios.",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "architecture-source",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 430,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 350,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "planned-boundary",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Planned, not implemented\nSteps 1–10 describe the intended controlled runner. They are a design model, not a claim about the current build.",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "trust-source",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "docs/product-strategy/TRUST_AND_EXECUTION_BOUNDARY.md",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 1360,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 380,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "layers-source",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "docs/product-strategy/PRODUCT_LAYERS.md",
      "x": -1200,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 380,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "analyst-contract",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Analyst-approved contract\nThe analyst defines:\n- legal input addresses;\n- labels, units, and types;\n- allowed values and ranges;\n- observed outputs;\n- validation and reconciliation cells;\n- compatible workbook identity.\n\nThe runtime applies the contract; it does not rediscover intent.",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 500,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "failure-posture",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Fail-closed conditions\nStop and do not certify the run when:\n- workbook identity is unexpected;\n- a mapped sheet or cell is missing;\n- a formula or protected cell would be overwritten;\n- incompatible scenarios are active;\n- Excel calculation fails;\n- validation or reconciliation fails;\n- restoration cannot be verified.\n\nDiagnostic evidence may remain, but a failed run is not a certified scenario.",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 1050,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 650,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "scenario-output",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Scenario package\nA downstream presentation tool receives only the deliberate package:\n- baseline and scenario identity;\n- approved inputs and outputs;\n- differences and time series;\n- units and evidence status;\n- validation status;\n- approved explanatory notes.\n\nGCBS presents the decision; it does not reinterpret the entire workbook.",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 2040,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 550,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-boundary",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Optional AI boundary\nAI may assist at design time with candidate levers, formula explanations, labels, tests, and narrative drafts. The analyst approves the map.\n\nThe trusted runtime remains deterministic and fully useful with AI disabled.",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 2780,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "3"
    }
  ],
